---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site.js';

const title = `Privacy · ${SITE.name}`;
const description =
  'No accounts, no tracking cookies, no consent banner. Cookieless analytics in production when configured, edge request logs, and nothing else — the whole list.';

const UPDATED = '2026-08-05';
---

<Base {title} {description}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      There is nothing to sign up for here, so there is not much to tell. This page is the whole
      list, including the parts that are true of any website.
    </p>

    <h2>What the site stores on your device</h2>
    <p>
      One thing: your light or dark theme choice, in <code>localStorage</code> under the key{' '}
      <code>theme</code>. It stays in your browser, it is not a cookie, and it is never sent
      anywhere. There is no tracking cookie, no consent banner to dismiss, and nothing stored about
      what you read, copy, or expand.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      In production, when the deployment is configured with a site ID, the site loads{' '}
      <a href="https://datafa.st" rel="noopener">DataFast</a> — cookieless analytics. It counts page
      views and referrers, plus a coarse country and device type derived from the request. It sets no
      cookie, and there is no cross-site profile to join.
    </p>
    <p>
      No site ID means no script at all: local development and preview builds load nothing
      third-party. Nothing you type, copy, or paste into a page reaches it, because there is nothing
      on this site to type into. Fonts and scripts are served from this domain, so no CDN learns you
      were here by handing you a typeface.
    </p>

    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare serves these pages and keeps request logs — IP address, user agent, timestamp, URL
      — for delivery, caching, and abuse handling. That is inherent to being served by anyone over
      the internet rather than a choice this site makes on top. We take no per-visitor log out of it
      and do not want one.
    </p>
    <p>
      This site is prerendered static pages. There is no login, no session, no user record, and no
      database of readers to leak.
    </p>

    <h2>What ships next, and what it will store</h2>
    <p>
      Outcome reports — worked, partly, failed — are planned on project pages, so that "reported
      working by readers" can mean something countable. When that form ships, a report row stores the
      project, the version, your OS, the agent you used, and your note. It stores nothing about your
      host: no IP address, no domain, no hostname, no credential, and no output from your install.
      Rate limiting happens at the edge and is not kept with the report. There is no email field,
      because there is no mailing list.
    </p>
    <p>
      When that ships, this page changes first. If this page and the code ever disagree, that is a
      bug worth reporting.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      No accounts means there is no profile to export or delete. For anything else, open an{' '}
      <a href={`${SITE.repoUrl}/issues/new/choose`} rel="noopener">issue</a> — including "your
      privacy page is wrong about your own stack", which would be a correction like any other.
    </p>

    <p class="provenance">
      Last updated {UPDATED}. Changes to this page are commits, and the{' '}
      <a href={`${SITE.repoUrl}/commits/main/src/pages/privacy.astro`} rel="noopener">file
      history</a> is the changelog.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 68ch;
    padding-block: 3rem 4rem;
  }
  .prose h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5em;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .provenance {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
</style>
